# =====================================================================================
# one_law_per_rung.rq — the one-law-per-child tooth (W2 · SP0, T-REDUCT).
# =====================================================================================
# Re-homes algebra_spine.ttl:99-103 constraints B (no-cram, <=1) + C (at-least-one, >=1)
# into the folded stratified idiom (design §3, §1.9): every concrete rung adds EXACTLY ONE
# law over its parent, made a graph fact on the reduct records (reducts.ttl) via @rel:adds:law.
#
# A reduct record (rec:reduct:record) is the forgetful morphism child|->parent; @rel:adds:law
# names the SINGLE law the child adds over that parent. This probe returns every reduct whose
# @rel:adds:law count != 1 — a reduct with TWO distinct @rel:adds:law CRAMS two laws (constraint B
# RED) and one with ZERO is a rung stripped of its added law (constraint C RED). The OPTIONAL +
# GROUP BY + HAVING catches BOTH bounds in one query (count 0 and count >=2 both != 1).
#
# GREEN over reducts.ttl: all seven reducts carry exactly one @rel:adds:law -> 0 rows.
# RED demonstration: give any reduct a second @rel:adds:law (cram) or strip its @rel:adds:law
# (starve) -> that reduct is returned. Runs via rdflib over the raw graph (no inference needed;
# the reduct types + @rel:adds:law edges are explicit in reducts.ttl).

PREFIX rec: <urn:silmaril:type:graph:instance:instruction:code:property:grounding:ontology:basic:formal:domain:knowledge:representation:kingdom:specification:phylum:formal:contract:class:class:order:declared:family:seed:genus:registry:species:>
PREFIX rel: <urn:silmaril:type:graph:instance:instruction:code:property:relation:>

SELECT ?reduct (COUNT(?law) AS ?laws) WHERE {
  ?reduct a rec:reduct:record .
  OPTIONAL { ?reduct rel:adds:law ?law . }
}
GROUP BY ?reduct
HAVING (COUNT(?law) != 1)
